WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.217
- I bet you've never heard that before.

00:00:03.217 --> 00:00:05.830
- No, no one's ever
said that to me before.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.130
Do you like warm hugs?

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.824
- I like to be unique, Josh.

00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:09.689
- What is that from?

00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:10.763
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:10.763 --> 00:00:13.128
- Is that the line that
people say the most to you?

00:00:13.128 --> 00:00:14.920
- It is.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.040
They say I like warm hugs
or they'll come up to me

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.790
and they'll say, do you
want to build a snowman?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.100
- Oh yeah.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.960
- My son just goes summer.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.536
He just comes out saying summer.

00:00:27.536 --> 00:00:29.616
He doesn't know the whole
song 'cause he's five.

00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:30.584
(Josh laughing)

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:31.420
But he'll just go, summer!,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.670
and it's just he's five and it's awesome.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:34.503
- Just randomly.

00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:35.336
- Just summer.

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:36.190
- Even if its in the dead of winter.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.023
- Yes, yip.

00:00:37.023 --> 00:00:38.920
He just loves the song but
he doesn't know the words.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:39.928
(Kelly and Josh laughing)

00:00:39.928 --> 00:00:41.560
Oh, well last time we saw each other,

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.393
you surprised me.

00:00:42.393 --> 00:00:43.608
And Sean Astin from the Goonies.

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:44.441
- Yes.

00:00:44.441 --> 00:00:46.680
So I'm just wondering who
you might've brought today.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.900
Cause I just, did you bring
anyone cool this time?

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.240
- Why am I never enough for
you is the real question.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.080
- You are but you really surprise me.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.746
- I know.
- It took me a minute,

00:00:56.746 --> 00:00:57.689
I was like is this Sean Astin,

00:00:57.689 --> 00:01:00.023
then I was like, oh I freaked out.

00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:01.290
I'm in the middle of Montana,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.462
in the middle of nowhere
when I got to meet a Goonie.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:04.430
- Well, we've talked about this.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.380
So Goonies is like our
mutual favorite movie

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.470
of all times.
- Yes, yes.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.770
- And then I did like an actual
table read with those guys

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.603
- I know.

00:01:12.603 --> 00:01:15.287
- where I played Sloth because right.

00:01:15.287 --> 00:01:16.712
- Shut up.

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:17.720
- So it was,

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.830
he's amazing and I didn't
bring anyone for you today.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.798
I hope this works for you guys.

00:01:22.798 --> 00:01:24.389
- This is enough, you are enough.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:25.995
You are enough.

00:01:25.995 --> 00:01:28.630
Has anyone ever
surprised... 'cause I loved

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:29.490
that I still get,

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.080
like still 20 years in this career

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.030
Like I still get so excited.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:33.990
I'm not jaded at all.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.720
I get very excited about meeting people.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.500
Has anybody ever surprised you like that?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.837
- Yes, my.

00:01:38.837 --> 00:01:42.020
We're very lucky. I got to
meet like so many cool people

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.560
but the one that really won me over

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.750
was for my 40th birthday
which I celebrated last year.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.260
I got for my birthday,

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.810
a special video from Cameo.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.357
My friends got me a message from Ken Bone.

00:01:56.357 --> 00:01:57.989
Ken bone was the guy,

00:01:57.989 --> 00:02:00.520
and I became obsessed
with him for some reason,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.900
- Who's Ken Bone?

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.299
- I'm going to, well that's
what I'm about to tell you.

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:05.132
(audience laughing)

00:02:05.132 --> 00:02:09.800
So Ken Bone was the guy in
like the 2016 election time,

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.000
there was a debate

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.960
and this one very special
man from the audience

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.230
was wearing this tight sweater
you guys remember this?

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.660
He had like this sweater and he just was,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.080
he just completely and
boom that's Ken Bone.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.241
Thank you to your crew
for showing you Ken Bone.

00:02:26.241 --> 00:02:27.400
- (Kelly laughing)

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.110
So I became obsessed,

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.630
so that he knew I was obsessed

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.263
and they got him to deliver
a message for my birthday.

00:02:34.263 --> 00:02:36.980
And it was just, that was so wonderful.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.290
- I love that you have met
so many amazing people.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.603
- Steven Spielberg,

00:02:41.603 --> 00:02:43.840
just like every pop star
and I'm like Ken Bone.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.020
- Ken Bone. (laughing)

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.230
That's amazing.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.063
- Barbara Streisand?

00:02:48.063 --> 00:02:48.896
Yes I've met her.

00:02:48.896 --> 00:02:50.030
- Yes, Ken Bone.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.374
- We talk about Ken Bone.

00:02:51.374 --> 00:02:53.039
(laughing)

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.740
- That's amazing.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.540
- Wait, so how old are your kids now?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.670
- So my kids are...

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.670
- One of them is my daughter's age.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.929
- Yes, yes.

00:03:00.929 --> 00:03:04.760
- One, one of them is seven, Izzy.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.980
The other one is just turned 11

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.840
and Izzy's in a little bit
of a lying phase right now,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.990
which I don't know if
you're going through.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.250
- Does she, does she say,
oh no, I was just faking.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.730
- Yes! I was just faking.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.417
She says, oh just
kidding or just faking it

00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:23.900
and I'm like no, you're clinically lying.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.440
- You're a pathological liar.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.656
You're sick. This is a sickness.

00:03:28.656 --> 00:03:29.489
(audience laughing)

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:30.322
But it'll be like,

00:03:30.322 --> 00:03:31.450
it'll be random stuff.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.283
- Dumb stuff.

00:03:32.283 --> 00:03:33.116
- Dumb stuff.
- Yep.

00:03:33.116 --> 00:03:36.630
Like you just went to the
bathroom and forgot to flush

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.460
and she'll be like, no.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.293
And I'll be like,

00:03:39.293 --> 00:03:41.719
I haven't done anything
that small since I was four.

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:43.080
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.859
So like, I know it's not me.

00:03:45.859 --> 00:03:48.628
Your sister's not home.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:51.070
Like it's not your mom.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:53.330
So like, it's you.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.390
And she'll be like, I don't
know what you're talking about.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.730
And then I'll like,

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.100
I'll find a way to prove it
and she'll go, just kidding.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.700
- I hate that.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.060
I was just faking. I'm
like, no, no, no, no.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.370
It's just called lying

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.120
- Yes, exactly.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.520
- It's just hard sometimes,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.520
like how do you get them to stop?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.438
I don't know if you find
out the phone a friend,

00:04:12.438 --> 00:04:15.410
but you shared an awesome moment
with your family recently.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:18.270
I love this moment as well, let's see it.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.650
- [Josh] Come on girls.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.150
I got a surprise for you guys.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.493
- Right there.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.083
- Grandma!

00:04:27.956 --> 00:04:29.762
(laughing)

00:04:29.762 --> 00:04:32.429
(kids shouting)

00:04:40.598 --> 00:04:41.646
(audience clapping)

00:04:41.646 --> 00:04:44.076
- I mean, that's how long two years?

00:04:44.076 --> 00:04:45.076
- Two years.

00:04:47.722 --> 00:04:50.016
- That's so sad, that's
like so many families though

00:04:50.016 --> 00:04:51.120
because of COVID.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.040
- Because of COVID,

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.590
they hadn't seen their
grandparents in two years

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.713
and I wanted to surprise them.

00:04:56.713 --> 00:05:00.440
And I was away shooting in London

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.990
a project up until last week.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:04.060
And so I surprised them as well.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.840
So it was like just surprise overload.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.330
And there you didn't see it on the video,

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.280
but the tears in their eyes,

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.690
just the pure joy in
their eyes was so amazing

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:15.720
and so incredible

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.920
and I know everybody here and elsewhere

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:19.980
has had this experience,

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.550
but it's just like losing that contact,

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.950
losing that proximity was so tough.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.810
- Not only for your kids,
especially the grandparents.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:28.810
I know my mom was like,

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.313
I feel like they grow
so fast at these ages.

00:05:31.313 --> 00:05:32.146
- A hundred percent.

00:05:32.146 --> 00:05:32.979
- So it's like,

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:33.812
I feel like I missed out that's you know,

00:05:33.812 --> 00:05:34.873
my mom had said that.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.300
- It was, it was incredible.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.790
- Well, I could talk about
your family the whole show,

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.532
'cause I love your
family and so do my kids.

00:05:40.532 --> 00:05:41.407
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.504
So what is Wolf Like Me about?

00:05:43.504 --> 00:05:48.123
- Wolf Like Me is about a
character named Boba Fett

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.166
who is just kidding.

00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:53.710
- I was like what. (laughing)

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.684
- Just wanted to make
sure paying attention,

00:05:56.684 --> 00:05:57.517
Woo woo!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.580
Just wanted to make sure
everybody was paying attention.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.070
- I'm on.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:06.100
- So Wolf Like Me,

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:09.610
it's an amazing story
between these two characters

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:10.970
named Mary and Gary,

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.510
both going through very
difficult periods of their lives.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.209
My character Gary is a single father

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.840
and he just,

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.780
things have happened in his
life that have been tough

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:24.150
and his daughter who's 12 years
old is going through a rough

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.580
patch and he's closed off

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.230
and then he has this sudden encounter

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.340
with this woman named Mary

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.810
and the two quite literally
and metaphorically

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.900
crash into each other's lives.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:40.690
And this is a story about
how difficult love can be

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:45.210
and also how much baggage
we bring into relationships.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.043
- Hmm.

00:06:46.043 --> 00:06:46.980
- But it's done through the prism

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.330
of some really exciting
and cool genre stuff

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.630
that I can't talk about
- Because then you'll ruin it.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:53.650
- because then I'll ruin it.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.120
But it is one of the
most incredible things

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.670
I've ever been a part of.
It is just so wonderful.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.990
Abe Forsyth who directed me

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.740
in a movie called Little
Monsters that I did

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.660
with Lupita Nyong'o directed this as well.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.540
And he calls me up and he goes,
Josh, I've got the script.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.260
This is an Australian accent right now,

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.712
(laughing)

00:07:14.712 --> 00:07:16.293
in case you were like,
what's happening now.

00:07:16.293 --> 00:07:17.157
- Well you have to point it out

00:07:17.157 --> 00:07:18.210
I don't know if you're nailing it.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.060
- No, they know, they know, anyways

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.942
he says, yeah, yeah, Dingo.

00:07:21.942 --> 00:07:24.608
(Kelly laughing)

00:07:24.608 --> 00:07:26.250
He calls me up and he said Josh,

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.790
I've got this project.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:30.670
It's going to go next month in Australia.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:31.503
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:07:31.503 --> 00:07:32.710
- You and Esla Fisher,

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:33.730
who I love,
- Love.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:34.820
- obsessed.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:38.990
And you would have to fly
here quarantine for two weeks

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.840
and then we shoot for
three and a half months.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.018
- Sounds like a party.

00:07:42.018 --> 00:07:43.130
- And I was like,

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:46.500
I don't know I'm sort of like a father.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:49.740
So like that's not a good idea right now.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.120
And he's like,

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.020
just read the script and I read the script

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:54.337
and I am telling you,

00:07:54.337 --> 00:07:57.309
I got to the end of the first episode

00:07:57.309 --> 00:08:01.300
and then I immediately
tore through the next five

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:02.270
and was like, I'm in.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.207
I have to do it.

00:08:03.207 --> 00:08:04.410
- I love it, it's that
powerful that's cool.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.920
- It's incredible.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:06.854
But it was great.

00:08:06.854 --> 00:08:10.300
I think everyone will
find that it was worth it

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.533
to abandon my family.

00:08:11.533 --> 00:08:13.271
(laughing)

00:08:13.271 --> 00:08:14.440
- Be a dead beat father

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.695
so that you could all be entertained.

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.561
- Oh my god I love you so much.

00:08:18.561 --> 00:08:20.170
So you did it in Australia.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.580
I love Australia. Did
you see any wildlife?

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.070
Like, cause y'all shot in
like the Outback, right.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.600
- So when you go to the Outback,

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.674
what do you expect to see?

00:08:27.674 --> 00:08:28.590
- Well kangaroo's?

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.640
- Kangaroo.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.441
Not a damn kangaroo.

00:08:31.441 --> 00:08:32.314
(audience laughing)

00:08:32.314 --> 00:08:33.360
- Not one?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.540
- Not one.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.550
Not only that I would get
to set at like 5:00 AM,

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.890
5:00 AM or 4:30 in the morning.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:43.000
And I get there and my
makeup artists would be like,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:43.833
did you see the kangaroos?

00:08:43.833 --> 00:08:44.933
- I knew that was going to happen.

00:08:44.933 --> 00:08:45.766
- And it was like, no.

00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:47.146
She goes, oh you must come in too late.

00:08:47.146 --> 00:08:49.519
I'm like, it's 4:30 in the morning.

00:08:49.519 --> 00:08:51.080
(laughing)

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.220
What kind of (beep) do the
kangaroo's have to get to

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.123
that they're like sorry, I'm running late.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.520
4:30 AM you got into late.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.480
So it was always like,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.490
I feel like it's a conspiracy.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.100
- Like, so everyone else.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:11.690
- Everyone saw kangaroo's
and then Esla pointed one out

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.334
and it was like 30 miles away.

00:09:14.334 --> 00:09:15.299
(laughing)

00:09:15.299 --> 00:09:17.066
It could have just as easily

00:09:17.066 --> 00:09:19.990
been a man in a kangaroo outfit.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:20.823
- Like a bunny.

00:09:20.823 --> 00:09:23.330
- Like just a large bunny,

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.760
a very unhealthy bunny
jumping in the distance.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:29.000
- I want to ask you this cause
you've done so much Broadway

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.050
that you've forgotten your lyrics, right.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.410
I've heard that you kind of did on stage

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.196
and people think it's kind
of a fun thing with you.

00:09:34.196 --> 00:09:35.936
- Yeah, though it's not.

00:09:35.936 --> 00:09:37.363
(laughing)

00:09:37.363 --> 00:09:40.880
It's not a fun thing. That's a nightmare.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.780
- I know I'm bad at it too. Are you?

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.580
How are you at it though?
Cause here's my thing.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:48.900
Somehow I will say something
it will somehow rhyme,

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.540
it won't make sense, but
it will somehow rhyme.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.700
- So that's what you're taught to do.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:56.396
What's interesting is I did not do that.

00:09:56.396 --> 00:09:57.941
(laughing)

00:09:57.941 --> 00:10:02.941
I took the opposite approach
and forgot the human language,

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:06.990
forgot the entirety of
our experience vocally

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:09.082
as a collective species

00:10:09.082 --> 00:10:11.820
and just stopped talking

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:15.440
as the music was playing very loudly.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.700
It gets worse.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:22.500
The stage manager was
screaming the line at me

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.040
going you're making things up again.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:29.473
And all I heard was eeeeee.

00:10:29.473 --> 00:10:30.306
- What.

00:10:30.306 --> 00:10:34.053
I had like tinnitus or I
was a living nightmare.

00:10:34.053 --> 00:10:34.886
- Oh you had like a ringing?

00:10:34.886 --> 00:10:36.720
- I had like a ringing sensation.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.063
- I've had that happen once to me.

00:10:38.063 --> 00:10:39.180
- It was like,

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:43.370
it was like energy up above got
bored that day and was like,

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.660
let's play with Josh's life.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.440
And it was like, this is insane.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:51.960
And then my co-star was
screaming the line at me

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.490
and I still couldn't say the line.

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:55.560
I couldn't hear anything.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.240
And then can I curse on your show?

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.073
- We'll bleep it.

00:10:58.073 --> 00:10:58.990
You'll bleep it out, good.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:01.600
This is how I got out of it, okay.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:02.700
Live theater,

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.150
people paying $500 a ticket
to see Book of Mormon.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.430
I looked out at my cast and said,

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.196
What the (beep) is my next line.

00:11:10.196 --> 00:11:11.199
(laughing)

00:11:11.199 --> 00:11:14.199
(audience clapping)

00:11:15.596 --> 00:11:17.929
I am a trained professional.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.690
Don't try that at home.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:24.070
- But you know what if I'm at that show,

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.040
best experience ever.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.467
- But here's, here's the worst part.

00:11:28.467 --> 00:11:30.830
They were so confused.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.560
They weren't even enjoying it.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:33.628
They were just like,

00:11:33.628 --> 00:11:37.943
this is a very weird part
of this show right now

00:11:37.943 --> 00:11:40.270
does this happen every night?

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.510
This script feels like it needs work.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.490
And from that point on, in Book of Mormon,

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.610
I actually in the song,

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.930
I had an actual book of Mormon

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:54.890
where I pasted the lines so
that when I opened it up,

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:56.573
I don't care now
- That's clever.

00:11:56.573 --> 00:11:57.438
- I did it 10 years ago, whatever

00:11:57.438 --> 00:11:59.457
whatever audience, you
saw it after the fact.

00:11:59.457 --> 00:12:01.965
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:12:01.965 --> 00:12:03.113
- Spoiler alert.

00:12:03.113 --> 00:12:04.446
- Spoiler alert.

00:12:05.661 --> 00:12:06.494
- That's clever.

00:12:06.494 --> 00:12:08.200
- I know and then from then,

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.553
because then you get in your
head and you're like oh,

00:12:09.553 --> 00:12:10.897
it's going to happen again.

00:12:10.897 --> 00:12:12.680
Always when I watch the voice,

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.030
I'm always like so nervous,

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.910
'cause the kids are learning
it like every week, new songs.

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.470
- Dude, they just, they learn
it like quickly like that.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.610
That's why it's hard to do but anyway,

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:22.910
I struggle a lot with lyrics.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.240
I have, since I was a kid,

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.160
like I don't have a really
great memory in general

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:26.993
when it comes to stuff like that.

00:12:26.993 --> 00:12:29.680
So I figured since you
suck and I suck at this,

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.741
we should play a game and who's the worst.

00:12:31.741 --> 00:12:32.649
(laughing)

00:12:32.649 --> 00:12:33.482
- Great, yes.

00:12:33.482 --> 00:12:34.315
(audience cheering)

00:12:34.315 --> 00:12:35.981
Yes.
- Does that sound like fun?

00:12:35.981 --> 00:12:36.932
- Yes please.

